    "UIName": "Fafnir",
    "Id": "chassisdef_fafnir_FNR-Z",
    "Name": "Fafnir",
    "Details": "Developed alongside the Society's experimental Heavy Gauss Rifle program, the FNR-Z began with a simple premise: rather than construct an entirely new BattleMech around the weapon, adapt a proven design already built to carry two of them. The Fafnir provided an ideal foundation, but Society scientists saw little reason to leave the rest of the machine untouched. Clan Endo Steel and Ferro-Lamellor armor were incorporated alongside a Society Light Engine with an integrated Supercharger, substantially improving both protection and mobility. A Society torso-mounted Direct Neural Interface and Nova CEWS further modernize the design, while a pair of Medium Supra Lasers and a Clan Medium Pulse Laser provide secondary firepower. Most importantly, the FNR-Z mounts a pair of Society Heavy Gauss Rifles, with prototype Nano-Fluid Dampers employed to tame their tremendous recoil. Given the volatile nature of both systems, Clan CASE II was installed to contain the inevitable consequences should the armor fail. The result is less a reinvention of the Fafnir than the Society's answer to a simple question: if the original concept already worked, why not make it better?\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Stable Weapons</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.18</color></b>\n\n<color=#FFEF00>Arm Actuator Limits: Left Upper, Right Upper</color>",
    "Icon": "Fafnir"
  },
